  "reason": "The only strong signal so far is RNA-only PCA singleprofile, which substantially outperforms image-only ResNet in both accuracy and F1. The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation can improve this promising RNA baseline without changing the representation. config_002 keeps the same RNA encoder and modality, testing only the shift to multiprofile with average pooling. This is a low-confound, efficient next step: it exploits the current best direction while clarifying whether profile aggregation is worth further investment before testing more complex encoders, transformers, or multimodal fusion."
